//! The Rust deterministic-simulation runner (spec/design/simulation-testing.md). It executes `.sim`
//! traces generated by scripts/sim_gen.rb against a Database over the simulated disk ([`disk`]),
//! checks the oracles of §8, and writes a transcript the driver (scripts/sim.rb) compares across
//! cores. A function-by-function port of the Go reference (`impl/go/sim_runner_test.go`): the
//! transcripts of the two must be byte-identical for every trace.
//!
//! Test-only, compiled under the non-default `sim` cargo feature and run through the `sim` binary:
//!
//! ```text
//! JED_SIM_IN=trace.sim JED_SIM_OUT=out/ cargo run --release --features sim --bin sim
//! ```
//!
//! `JED_SIM_IN` is one .sim file, a directory of them, or a file listing trace paths one per line.
//! Results append to `JED_SIM_RESULTS` (default `JED_SIM_OUT/rust.results.jsonl`). With
//! `JED_SIM_IMAGES` set, every image a recovery opens is written to
//! `JED_SIM_OUT/<trace>.rust.step<N>.img` for the independent checker.

